      "content": "everything you're saying sounds like a textbook. \"grief\" \"trauma\" \"professional support\"... it's all just words to help people pretend things aren't broken. but they are. they're broken. if you're at a casino and you've lost every single cent you ever had, no one tells you to \"rebuild\" your bankroll at the table. they just tell you it's over. they tell you to walk away so you stop losing. why is it so different when it's your actual life? why is it considered \"wrong\" to just accept that the game is over and stop playing?",
